WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.927
Here's what you'll be able to
do by the end of this module,

2
00:00:02.927 --> 00:00:05.175
which takes about sixty
minutes with Lab 1.

3
00:00:05.175 --> 00:00:08.462
You'll set up a forest for
G M S As in the right order.

4
00:00:08.462 --> 00:00:11.733
You'll say when the backdated
K D S key is allowed,

5
00:00:11.733 --> 00:00:13.913
and why a forest has only one key.

6
00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:18.675
You'll follow a new workload's G M S A
from the request to a working service.

7
00:00:18.675 --> 00:00:22.017
You'll decide whether a new
G M S A is outbound-only,

8
00:00:22.017 --> 00:00:25.275
and register an S P N when
the workload needs one.

9
00:00:25.275 --> 00:00:27.768
And you'll run Chapter 12's request check

10
00:00:27.768 --> 00:00:30.488
and Chapter 6's one-account
plan on fixtures.

11
00:00:30.488 --> 00:00:34.725
Before you start, finish Module 1
and read the standard's settings.

12
00:00:34.725 --> 00:00:40.580
You need PowerShell 7.1 or later with Pester
5, and no domain or tenant for Lab 1.
